        <definition>void ListeningSocket::shutdown</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>shutdown</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::ListeningSocket::shutdown</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Closes the FD, unlinks the socket file, and writes to PipeFD. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>After the construction of the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket" kindref="compound">ListeningSocket</ref>, shutdown is signal safe if it is called during the lifetime of the object. shutdown can be called concurrently with <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket_1ac080084a7f9f9a2d530621e41a309967" kindref="member">ListeningSocket::accept</ref> as writing to PipeFD will cause a blocking call to ::poll to return.</para>
<para>Once shutdown is called there is no way to reinitialize <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket" kindref="compound">ListeningSocket</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
