    <briefdescription>
<para>Manages a passive (i.e., listening) UNIX domain socket. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket" kindref="compound">ListeningSocket</ref> class encapsulates a UNIX domain socket that can listen and accept incoming connections. <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket" kindref="compound">ListeningSocket</ref> is portable and supports Windows builds begining with Insider Build 17063. <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket" kindref="compound">ListeningSocket</ref> is designed for server-side operations, working alongside <computeroutput>raw_socket_streams</computeroutput> that function as client connections.</para>
<para>Usage example: <programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">std::string<sp/><ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1pdb_1ac10322dc19a928c2dbb83ec9689dc23caac70412e939d72a9234cdebb1af5867b" kindref="member">Path</ref><sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;/path/to/socket&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Expected&lt;ListeningSocket&gt;<sp/>S<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_listening_socket_1a22cd57e089541409aa05153237a44729" kindref="member">ListeningSocket::createUnix</ref>(Path);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(S)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>Expected&lt;std::unique_ptr&lt;raw_socket_stream&gt;&gt;<sp/>connection<sp/>=<sp/>S-&gt;accept();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(connection)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Use<sp/>the<sp/>accepted<sp/>raw_socket_stream<sp/>for<sp/>communication.</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
